        "id": 1002124
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-01-20T16:58:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We appear to be ignoring all the return values. So why provide them?",
      "revId": "5cd8dd5bb50f1a0d3a8f1eb1424e9450a0c9870d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4beecfc7_2dae2d29",
        "filename": "util/comm-lpc.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 31,
      "author": {
        "id": 1111479
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-01-21T07:40:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "While we are porting this change to flashrom, https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/#/c/236781, we felt that it was important to add an error return code when accessing EC, especially during a flash option.\n\nAs for ectool, I am trying to minimize change as much as possible in this patch, so I am modifying the code to use only this new macro without adding new code to make use of the return value. We can do this as a future enhancement.",
      "parentUuid": "0b4a1799_24c3d86d",
      "revId": "5cd8dd5bb50f1a0d3a8f1eb1424e9450a0c9870d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
